{
  "summary": "Replaces the directory-scoped `include_directories` call in `src/CMakeLists.txt` with target-scoped `target_include_directories` on `core_interface`. Links `bitcoin_ipc` against `core_interface` so `ipc/stub.cpp` inherits project build flags, and removes the custom `WarnAboutGlobalProperties` module now that native CMake checks cover it.",
  "problem": "Directory-level directives like `include_directories` trigger `-Wnon-target-directive` warnings starting in CMake 4.5.0. Switching to target-scoped properties would leave the static `bitcoin_ipc` stub library missing project-wide build flags and includes unless explicitly linked to `core_interface`.",
  "evidence": [
    "CMake 4.5.0 warning output reproduced in description: \"CMake Warning (non-target-directive) at src/CMakeLists.txt:8 (include_directories): Use of non-target directives is not recommended. Consider target_include_directories instead.\"",
    "Commit 4ef05d6f45: \"Otherwise, `ipc/stub.cpp` is compiled without the project-wide build flags.\""
  ],
